  "purpose": "Disclosed book_concentration inputs for measure_book.py --live. Each row is the entity's DISCLOSED gross written premium split: total GWP plus the premium written in named energy/power (and any named data-centre/tech) lines, from a Lloyd's syndicate 'class of business' table or company segmental/SFCR reporting. NO synthetic values — leave an entity OUT until you have its real, sourced figures. The script skips any entity not present here.",
  "instructions": {
    "total_gwp": "total gross written premium (number, same currency as below)",
    "energy_power_gwp": "premium in named energy/power class(es) only. Use the NARROWEST named class; do NOT use broad Solvency II Fire/Property LoBs (they over-include).",
    "datacentre_tech_gwp": "premium in any named data-centre/tech class (optional; omit if not separately disclosed)",
    "currency": "e.g. 'GBP', 'USD' — units of the figures (millions assumed in rationale)",
    "lines_counted": "array of the exact class names you summed, e.g. ['Energy','Renewables']",
    "source": "primary URL to the syndicate annual report / segmental disclosure",
    "as_of": "YYYY-MM-DD reporting date",
    "applies_to": "risk-carriers only (insurer, lloyds_syndicate, reinsurer). Computed ONLY where a named energy/power premium is disclosed; otherwise book_concentration stays assessed."
  },
